# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — rewritten 2026-09-06 for the reorganised layout.
#
# LESSON ENCODED HERE: the previous file used unanchored directory rules like
# `unet_run_fixednorm/`, which match at ANY depth. After the reorganisation
# those silently swallowed the tracked metrics.json / training_log.csv files
# that had moved to runs/unet/unet_run_fixednorm/. Rules that mean "at the
# repo root" are now anchored with a leading slash. Also note git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so directories that
# contain anything worth tracking are never excluded wholesale — the heavy
# file TYPES are excluded instead.
# =============================================================================

# --- datasets and derived arrays: never in git -------------------------------
data/

# --- model weights and framework checkpoints, at any depth -------------------
*.pkl
*.pt
*.pth
*.h5
*.ckpt
model.ckpt.*
events.out.tfevents.*
**/checkpoint

# --- heavy run artefacts (the small metrics/logs beside them stay tracked) ---
runs/**/checkpoints/
runs/**/predictions/
runs/lofar/*/ckpt/
runs/lofar/*/best/
runs/prediction/
/prediction/
pred/

# --- large generated image sets ----------------------------------------------
docs/preview/
results/*.npy

# --- analysis working data ---------------------------------------------------
analysis/hera_transfer_test/HERA_npy/

# --- python / editor / os ----------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- copyrighted PDFs --------------------------------------------------------
RFI_Using_UNET.pdf

# --- misc --------------------------------------------------------------------
video_transcript_*.txt
